        "slide": 5,
        "role": "evidence",
        "subject": "A high plan oblique down the unroofed bay toward the open dock door, its warm spill fanning across twenty slab pads in four rows of five. The ten pads nearest the door are taped gold or rust and the ten nearest the camera are taped grey.",
        "visual_consequence": "Half the floor is warm and half is grey, split at one row line, and the warm half is nearest the door. At 432 px a reader can count two warm rows against two grey rows without the dek.",
        "weakness": "Nothing blocking and nothing changed since the accepted reading. Outside the spill the pads read as tape outlines with no slab edge, the grey tape inside the spill is warm tan close to the gold, and the open door shows a flat beige apron rather than sky.",
